[
    {
        "content": "<p>As of now, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRecOn#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRecOn</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.caseStrongRecOn#doc\">docs#Nat.caseStrongRecOn</a> are <code>noncomputable</code>.</p>\n<p>Would it be good to make them computable by upstreaming the code for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRecOn%27#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRecOn'</a> in mathlib, as shown below?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">elab_as_elim</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">strongRecOn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">aux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">not_lt_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_of_lt_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le_of_lt_succ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577319341,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1772646243
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As a related step I've opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36165\">#36165</a> (in mathlib) deprecating two lemmas equivalent to <em>Batteries</em> <code>Nat.strongRec</code></p>",
        "id": 577394707,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1772675022
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This feels quite desirable. If one is going to do this, I suppose the only question is that you'd want to do it in a way that generates efficient output ideally (or at least not egregiously inefficient).</p>",
        "id": 577412132,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1772686231
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I recently bumped into <code>Nat.strongRecOn'</code> and had to figure out the reason for why they are duplicated. I'd be great to unify them.</p>",
        "id": 577621050,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1772755391
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>BTW, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRecOn%27#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRecOn'</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRec%27#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRec'</a> can be defined more shortly by using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFounded.Nat.fix#doc\">docs#WellFounded.Nat.fix</a> directly.</p>\n<p>Maybe this can remove <code>set_option backward.privateInPublic true</code> in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRec%27#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRec'</a> .</p>",
        "id": 577648256,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1772768503
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRecOn#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRecOn</a> in Lean core could also use <code>WellFounded.Nat.fix</code> directly (modulo some reordering of declarations).</p>",
        "id": 577649115,
        "sender_full_name": "David Renshaw",
        "timestamp": 1772768977
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"243791\">David Renshaw</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Computability.20of.20.60Nat.2E.28case.29strongRecOn.60/near/577649115\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I believe <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.strongRecOn#doc\">docs#Nat.strongRecOn</a> in Lean core could also use <code>WellFounded.Nat.fix</code> directly (modulo some reordering of declarations).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm making <code>Nat.(case)strongRecOn</code> computable in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12894\">lean4#12894</a></p>",
        "id": 578830146,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1773289454
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">elab_as_elim</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">strongRecOn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578832412,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1773291120
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12894\">lean4#12894</a> now builds batteries and mathlib</p>",
        "id": 579178462,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1773373823
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd like <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12894\">lean4#12894</a> to be merged, please</p>",
        "id": 590605244,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1776997409
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"598052\">@Jeremy Tan</span>, you still haven't responded to Joachim/Markus's comments, asking for evidence that that annotations you've added give the expected behaviour.</p>",
        "id": 592876720,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1777946860
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110087\">Kim Morrison</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Computability.20of.20.60Nat.2E.28case.29strongRecOn.60/near/592876720\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"598052\">Jeremy Tan</span>, you still haven't responded to Joachim/Markus's comments, asking for evidence that that annotations you've added give the expected behaviour.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I sidestepped those comments</p>",
        "id": 592876748,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1777946885
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Otherwise I have no idea how to respond</p>",
        "id": 592876763,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1777946894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span> I have no idea how to respond to the comment</p>",
        "id": 592878447,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1777948009
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, I have removed the <code>@[macro_inline]</code>annotations per <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12894#discussion_r3136189672\">this other comment</a>. There are conflicting comments on whether the annotation helps or harms</p>",
        "id": 592878543,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1777948057
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"470149\">@Joachim Breitner</span> is contradicting himself on <code>@[macro_inline]</code>, that the <em>maintainers themselves</em> cannot agree on the annotation, and I am very confused</p>",
        "id": 592879347,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1777948558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You could try writing some code with these functions, and look at the IR the compiler produces, to get an idea of what <code>macro_inline</code> does, and then you can report your findings :)</p>",
        "id": 592908446,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777960469
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Computability.20of.20.60Nat.2E.28case.29strongRecOn.60/near/592908446\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You could try writing some code with these functions, and look at the IR the compiler produces, to get an idea of what <code>macro_inline</code> does, and then you can report your findings :)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>How do I find and analyse the IR again?</p>",
        "id": 600874768,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1780771807
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Where is the IR anyway?</p>",
        "id": 600874779,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1780771822
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can do <code>set_option trace.compiler.ir.result true in</code></p>",
        "id": 600875862,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780772693
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Some preliminary results (finally!) can be seen <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12894#issuecomment-4640118189\">here</a></p>",
        "id": 600877469,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1780773980
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, I have the results with both <code>@[inline]</code> and <code>@[macro_inline]</code> for a test snippet featuring <code>Nat.caseStrongRecOn</code> ready on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12894\">lean#12894</a></p>",
        "id": 600950835,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1780799018
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a very short test that shows that <code>macro_inline</code> works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFounded</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Strong induction on the natural numbers.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">The induction hypothesis is that all numbers less than a given number satisfy the motive, which</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">should be demonstrated for the given number.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">elab_as_elim</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">strongRecOn12894</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Case analysis based on strong induction for the natural numbers.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">elab_as_elim</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">macro_inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">caseStrongRecOn12894</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">strongRecOn12894</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lt_succ_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</s